WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.820
With the United Kingdom leaving the European
Union, it's natural to wonder what this means

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:07.549
for the EU going forward.
And there's really two different ways to think

00:00:07.549 --> 00:00:09.790
about it.
One, if you want to be optimistic about the

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:12.889
European project,
is that the EU could actually be stronger

00:00:12.889 --> 00:00:17.769
without the UK in it.
To understand how, it helps to look at the

00:00:17.769 --> 00:00:21.689
history of the EU
And the idea is to take this continent that

00:00:21.689 --> 00:00:26.089
is the cradle of a wonderful civilization,
but has also been the scene of some incredibly

00:00:26.089 --> 00:00:30.279
destructive wars, some horrific political
crimes, and make sure that kind of thing can

00:00:30.279 --> 00:00:34.970
never happen again.
And the idea was if they unified the steel

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:39.570
and coal industries across national boundaries,
they wouldn't be able to fight wars with one

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:44.870
another.
But the UK was never completely on board.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:47.430
They weren't one of the six original countries
to join up

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:53.000
they joined a little bit reluctantly, they
didn't want to join the single currency project.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:57.620
And English people have, in a geographic sense,
often not felt that they are even quote unquote

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:02.590
part of Europe. So, to an extent they've always
been the marginal member, and if anyone is

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:06.029
going to leave, it would be them.
Once the UK is out, the remaining

00:01:06.039 --> 00:01:10.350
countries might be able to get some important
things done, like crafting a common immigration

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:14.280
and foreign policy, which the EU doesn’t
have, and trying to figure out a way to make the

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:17.549
common currency work better.
They don’t have a common tax policy, they

00:01:17.549 --> 00:01:21.799
don’t have a common welfare state
It may be easier for the countries that remain

00:01:21.799 --> 00:01:27.369
to build stronger institutions,
And you may ultimately see a stronger, even

00:01:27.369 --> 00:01:30.219
though it’s a smaller Europe.
That’s the optimistic view

00:01:30.219 --> 00:01:34.369
Now, another view could be that we're looking
at the beginning of the unraveling of the

00:01:34.369 --> 00:01:39.789
whole thing.
You start pulling a thread on the sweater,

00:01:39.789 --> 00:01:44.039
and it's all going to collapse. You see polls
from France and even Germany, the countries

00:01:44.039 --> 00:01:47.619
at the very heart of Europe, showing that
it's become unpopular.

00:01:47.619 --> 00:01:50.719
They don’t feel ownership over European
politics.

00:01:50.719 --> 00:01:55.679
It's a bunch of guys, sitting around in a
Belgian city, negotiating deals in a language

00:01:55.679 --> 00:01:59.530
they don't speak.
They don’t have a spirit of European patriotism

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:06.350
and a deep, emotional European identity.
The EU has a lot of the attributes of a nation state.

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:11.330
It has a flag, they have a national anthem, but it doesn't have any words.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:16.800
If you fielded a single EU soccer team, it would
win the World Cup every time, but no one would cheer for it.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:23.400
So, a lot of how this turns in the end has to do with what kind of deal the UK can reach with the EU.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:27.620
If the UK manages to get out but to then still have a really favorable free trade

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:32.160
deal with the EU and really sort of prosper, that's going to make it easier for other countries

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.740
to say well, they want out too every time

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.740
a decision happens that they don't like.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:42.780
So there's a strong incentive  to make this messy, to make it really as painful as possible.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:48.960
If EU leaders manage to exact a high price from the UK in leaving, that means that probably

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:51.940
the rest of the union is not going to break up.

